# Routing and Layout

- Define route paths in a shared constants module and reuse them for route config, links, and redirects.
- Use React Router v6 route objects/components consistently; avoid ad-hoc path strings in pages.
- Lazy-load page routes with `React.lazy` and wrap with `Suspense` fallbacks suitable for dashboard UX.
- Wrap routes with the required layout shell (navigation/header/content container) instead of duplicating layout markup in pages.
- Keep guards/redirect logic near routing definitions, not scattered across page components.
- Keep route params and query parsing typed and validated before use in data fetching.
